= The Last Majles

## Iran, 1949–1953

Iran has a constitution, elections, a parliament, political parties, and a
mobilized public. It does not have a settled distribution of power.

You will represent the coordinating leadership of the National Front as it
tries to secure representative government and Iranian control of the oil
industry without losing the coalition and institutions needed to make either
achievement durable.

