@prototype_briefing
new-page: true

= October 1949

The elections to the Sixteenth Majles are being manipulated. Mohammad
Mossadegh and a small group of opposition figures prepare to seek sanctuary
at the royal palace and demand genuinely representative elections.

The eventual game will begin here. Its first playable slice will ask the
player to turn this protest into a working coalition, contest the elections,
and decide how a constitutional opposition should respond to a monarchy that
possesses both formal powers and informal instruments of influence.

This technical build confirms the project structure and build pipeline. No
campaign systems or historical choices have been implemented yet.

